  "term": "auditory feedback",
  "definition": "In psychology, auditory feedback can mean giving a person information about their own autonomic nervous system activity as sound, such as signals linked to heartbeat, brain waves, or skin temperature. It is used in biofeedback to help the person learn some self-control over related conditions.",
